  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 acc, far exceeding both image-only baselines (~0.21-0.23), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA) in one profile setting, leaving it unclear whether the 0.485 ceiling is due to the linear PCA representation or is inherent to the RNA signal. Question: config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder (learned nonlinear latent representation vs. linear PCA) while holding profile setting constant. Why this is best: The encoder choice is the most fundamental design decision—it will influence every downstream multimodal and multiprofile experiment. If scvi_n200 substantially outperforms PCA, it signals that learned representations are critical and justifies investing in scgpt and multimodal variants with better encoders. If it performs similarly or worse, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects the search toward profile/aggregation/fusion. This single experiment reduces the most consequential uncertainty with minimal confounding, making it the highest-information next step under a tight budget."
}

